	"_about": "Camera pitch and roll from a gravity vector: the cases common/capture_pose.py, the web app's level indicator (frontend/src/lib/capturePoseMath.ts) and frontend2 must agree on. gravity is the up vector in DEVICE coordinates (Android TYPE_GRAVITY: x right, y to the screen's top, z out of the screen), pitch and roll are GPano (positive up; roll from the nearest quarter turn, null within roll_floor of flat), and level is the indicator's verdict: 'level' passes both Panoramax gates, 'flat' has no roll. 'deviceorientation' adds the beta/gamma a browser reports for each vector. See docs/todo/web-capture-level-stamp.md.",
